WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:05.090
This is my favorite character in Jujutsu Kaisen
right now.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.090
I'm sorry.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:10.519
Remember, how I teased an Inumaki analysis
at the end of Nobara's video by making fun

00:00:10.519 --> 00:00:14.879
of how he says nothing but rice ball ingredients.

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:23.880
Well turns out it's really hard to analyze
a character based on that.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.990
- That poor guy.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:30.170
So instead, I'm gonna analyze a character
that I think is so well written and has such

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:40.550
a fantastic character arc, that you know she
is one of Akutami's favorites.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:45.560
What makes Maki so fun is that she was treated
like a dreadful case of bad breath by her

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.829
family, but rather than begging for acknowledgement
or affection, Maki has decided to tear the

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:53.809
whole abusive Zenin family to the ground.

00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:58.460
Of course this video will also be about Mai,
because, as you will see, both of them are

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.719
basically one character split into two.

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:05.750
There is a ton of symbolism around the concept
of twins here after all.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.280
And the story behind Maki and Mai is as tragic
as it is heartbreaking.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.390
And so it's no big surprise, that is is her
sister who is Maki's biggest flaw and weakness

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.100
as a character.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:24.170
At the same time however, she has also emerged
from her past as incredibly strong and fierce.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:30.390
I have already focus heavily on female writing
in Nobara's video, so I will not force it

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:35.689
here again, but it goes without saying that
Maki is exceptionally well written for Shounen

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:41.400
standards and I think in contrary to the beliefs
of at least some people in the industry, having

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.280
self-confident badasses like Kugisaki and
Maki makes everyone enjoy this story even

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.280
more.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.960
Because, as the manga readers will know, Maki
is here to stay and her character only gets

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.650
better better.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:10.640
This is the story of Zenin Maki.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:15.260
It's Maki's self-confident and indifferent
attitude, as well as her power in physical

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.370
combat that make it really easy to like her.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:22.640
As a matter of fact, she represents a lot
of the most common shounen tropes we like

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:28.201
to see in our heroes: A tragic past, Power
in combat, a seemingly unattainable gaol they

00:02:28.201 --> 00:02:33.360
want to reach, an iron determination to fight
for that goal as well as the ability to stick

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:40.069
through the toughest moments.

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:45.440
We see her fiercely and fearlessly wielding
a whole arsenal of cursed weapons, no matte

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.090
how strong the opponent she's facing.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.631
Maki is so extremely likable, because she
basically has all the characteristics, that

00:02:52.631 --> 00:03:05.519
our usual Shounen Hero has, only as a badass
girl.

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:11.270
She doesn't share any of the external struggles
and vulnerabilities that make Itadori so special,

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:16.879
and thus makes it extremely easy to latch
on to her, something we for example see Nobara

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:17.879
do.

00:03:17.879 --> 00:03:22.190
This is a woman that stands up against the
men who have suppressed her and fights for

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.650
becoming a powerful woman that can lead the
clan herself.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:36.879
Basically, her dream is showing everyone that
looked down on her one big middle finger.

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:42.629
- So it's very easy to see what makes her
so extremely cool to watch and follow.

00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:48.129
Other than Megumi, who internalizes the pain
caused by his family situation, Maki displays

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:54.150
her emotional damage openly to the world.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:59.570
And yet, I believe that the reasons Maki stands
out as a character, as with any great Character,

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:04.850
are the underlying flaws, unseeing symbols
and steady character progressions, that happen

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.989
beneath her straight-forward-feeling surface.

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:20.239
And Gege Akutami sure went full out when crafting
her character.

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:21.239
-

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:25.490
Maki and Mai were born as twin sisters to
the powerful Zenin clan, the most powerful

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:33.710
family in the Jujutsu world, if it weren't
for this guy right here, - who basically carries

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.639
the Gojo family on his own.

00:04:35.639 --> 00:04:41.289
As a result, Maki's and Mai's story isn't
only dramatic and sad in only way, but rather

00:04:41.289 --> 00:04:46.919
Akutami has piled a whole mountain of dramatic
layers of top of both of them, that weighs

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:52.039
down heavily on their lives, you know just
as American breakfast does.

00:04:52.039 --> 00:04:56.900
First of all, there is the fact that the Jujutsu
world operates based on very traditional and

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.120
conservative Japanese rules.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:04.500
Born into a powerful family, you are expected
to always put the clan's interest first.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:09.770
You have to be strong and flawless, serve
your elders and bring no shame onto the family

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.009
name.

00:05:11.009 --> 00:05:14.990
There is no room for personal feelings and
ambitions.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:20.969
On top of this, big surprise, in this conservative,
combat-oriented and patriarchal family structure,

00:05:20.969 --> 00:05:25.879
being born as a girl puts you on a harsh disadvantage
right from the start.

00:05:25.879 --> 00:05:30.310
You neither have the same social standing,
nor the same base physical strength of the

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:36.190
male family members, and so every woman has
to work at least twice as hard to be recognized

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:40.819
as a full-fledged sorcerer.

00:05:40.819 --> 00:05:49.389
Then, there is the fact that Maki and Mai
are twins, which for a long time were seen

00:05:49.389 --> 00:05:51.089
as a sign of misfortune in Japan.

00:05:51.089 --> 00:05:57.159
I even found this Japanese study that details
different types of food pregnant women were

00:05:57.159 --> 00:06:03.219
supposed to avoid to not bear twins, such
as twin chestnuts, double section tangerines

00:06:03.219 --> 00:06:06.389
or double eggplants.

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:12.999
Thus, being born a twin automatically made
you less worthy of love and trust.

00:06:12.999 --> 00:06:18.369
But as if all of this weren't enough already,
Maki and Mai actually also have to deal with

00:06:18.369 --> 00:06:21.619
real physical consequences of being twins
as well.

00:06:21.619 --> 00:06:26.580
Their cursed powers basically treated them
as one person as well, so that Mai ended up

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:32.179
with a uniquely strong cursed ability, but
no combat skills whatsoever, while Maki is

00:06:32.179 --> 00:06:37.809
one of the physically most gifted characters
in the story, but without so much as an ounce

00:06:37.809 --> 00:06:43.460
of cursed energy, which in the largest family
of jujutsu sorcerer, basically made her the

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.259
worst amongst the worst.

00:06:45.259 --> 00:06:51.030
As a result, both Maki and Mai grew up as
outcasts of the Zenin family, which left them

00:06:51.030 --> 00:07:02.609
with nothing but each other to hold onto.

00:07:02.609 --> 00:07:03.609
-

00:07:03.609 --> 00:07:07.939
Long story short Maki and Mai basically both
share the same fate of growing up abused and

00:07:07.939 --> 00:07:12.499
neglected by a family that only cares about
power.

00:07:12.499 --> 00:07:16.059
And yet, both of them deal with it in very
different ways.

00:07:16.059 --> 00:07:20.500
And while the story introduces us to Maki
as the mature, tough and straight forward

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:30.819
twin, Mai is presented as hateful, evil and
childish.

00:07:30.819 --> 00:07:34.210
And yet this perception is purposefully misleading.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:38.449
As I explained in my analysis of Nobara, as
we learn throughout their flashback, in the

00:07:38.449 --> 00:07:45.800
relationship of the twins, Maki is actually
the more hurtful one.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:51.349
Her big desire in life is paying back those
who abused her and her sister, who she always

00:07:51.349 --> 00:07:53.219
used to protect as a child.

00:07:53.219 --> 00:07:58.719
and yet in the process of struggling to get
stronger, she forgets about her sister completely,

00:07:58.719 --> 00:08:01.069
focusing fully on her goal.

00:08:01.069 --> 00:08:06.179
Mai on the other hand, never wanted to become
a sorcerer in the first place, she never had

00:08:06.179 --> 00:08:07.849
maki's mental strength.

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:13.069
All she wanted was having her big sister by
her side, the only family she had.

00:08:13.069 --> 00:08:19.099
And yet, through Maki's fight for power, she
herself has no choice but also become a sorcerer,

00:08:19.099 --> 00:08:24.419
or be left alone at the bottom of the clan.

00:08:24.419 --> 00:08:33.779
In addition, probably in an effort to protect
Mai from the consequences of going against

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:37.959
the Zenin clan, Maki severs her ties with
her sister.

00:08:37.959 --> 00:08:41.079
- however this hurts Mai even more.

00:08:41.079 --> 00:08:46.920
And while she finally finds comrades at the
Kyoto school, she never had Maki's conviction,

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.040
power or drive.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:53.240
As a result we hear her echoing a lot of the
opinions and behaviors around her, as she

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:58.520
doesn't have the confidence to form her own
opinions and forge her own path.

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:02.660
She's just letting herself be pulled along
by the stream of events around her.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:08.000
And the only way she now sees to get her sisters
attention is by taunting her or those close

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.660
to her, where she wants to be.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:12.660
-

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:21.060
The 
point here is, that very much in the spirit

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:26.560
of being twins, Maki and Mai are one person
split into two.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:31.410
Both dealing with their abusive family in
their own way and yet at the same time both

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.790
being a side of the same coin.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:41.280
Mai is insecure, weak-willed, averse to fighting,
emotional, but also has an extremely powerful

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:49.540
ability that allows her to create matter from
nothing.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.850
Even though she actually forms friendships
really fast, her whole life is determined

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.680
by her relationship with her sister.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:00.509
Her fault as a character then, fault from
a writing perspective of course, is relying

00:10:00.509 --> 00:10:05.829
on her and making her responsible for her
own feelings and events in her life.

00:10:05.829 --> 00:10:10.430
Mai's arc is about finding the determination
to fight back herself against the abuse and

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:15.500
oppression by her family and the jujutsu world,
side by side with her sister.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:21.240
Maki on the other hand, is strong, a fighter
and just like Gojo, thinks everything can

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:29.800
be solved by strength alone.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:34.560
And while strength surely is important in
the Jujutsu world, Maki has internalized a

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:39.250
ver unhealthy view of strength: not showing
any weakness.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:45.520
Maki blocks out her own emotions and insecurities
completely focusing mostly on herself.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:50.480
Similarly to Gojo, she knows the value of
having strong companions and being able to

00:10:50.480 --> 00:11:00.370
fight together, but in the end, her philosophy
is this - Gojo to Megumi.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:06.180
It’s not that Maki is a hateful person it’s
that she’s conditioned not to accept any

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:11.149
kind of love because she was never shown the
unconditional love of a family she was owed.

00:11:11.149 --> 00:11:16.620
She is so busy trying to reject everything
that the Zenin clan stands for, that she can’t

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:20.990
really accept other people’s feelings at
all positive or negative.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:27.579
She’s too busy thinking about herself, protecting
about herself, trying not to hate herself.

00:11:27.579 --> 00:11:30.310
She can't receive Mai's feelings.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:35.470
Again it's easy to draw a parallel to Megumi
here, who is not even blood-related to his

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:41.269
sister, but does everything he can for his
only real family member, desperately wanting

00:11:41.269 --> 00:11:42.879
to talk to her.

00:11:42.879 --> 00:11:53.160
- Maki however, despite having the chance
to talk to her twin sister and only real family

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.230
in the world whenever she wants, doesn't.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:12:02.689
Her having to wear glasses because she otherwise
is blind to curses is really symbolic here.

00:12:02.689 --> 00:12:08.249
Because these glasses also represent her inability
to see other people for who they are.

00:12:08.249 --> 00:12:13.379
If you watched my Gojo video, you will recognize
a pattern here.

00:12:13.379 --> 00:12:19.180
As a result, Maki's character arc is all about
understanding, that strength isn't always

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:25.199
the answer and that forming real relationships
with others, especially her own sister is

00:12:25.199 --> 00:12:28.380
an essential part of living a good life.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:33.680
And this also includes acknowledging and accepting
her sister's feelings and wishes into her

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:34.680
heart.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:38.490
And while her justified hatred towards her
family is a powerful drive for her growth

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:43.910
as a sorcerer, at some point after dealing
with the Zenin clan, she will need a more

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:48.529
healthy goal in life, that is not defined
by violence and hate, but that actually will

00:12:48.529 --> 00:12:56.209
do good in the world, or sink into deeper
darkness, as members of the Zenin family tend

00:12:56.209 --> 00:13:03.879
to do.

00:13:03.879 --> 00:13:10.050
One thing however is for certain, Maki already
being as strong as she is, with Mai by her

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:15.060
side, once again becoming one whole, she will
be a force to be reckoned with in the jujutsu

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:38.899
world, and no-one should underestimate her
power and role in the story.

